Sasha: Quick follow-up to the prefix caching RFC — proposing we decouple 'ownership' from 'residency' to simplify handoffs and reduce blocking during eviction. Draft: https://go/redwood/rfc/decouple-ownership. TL;DR: ownership token -> logical owner + epoch/fence; residency -> which node actually holds KV bytes + residency epoch. Handoff becomes mostly async, avoid synchronous blocking on eviction.

Maria: Interesting. How do we preserve RAWR (read-after-write) guarantees during async handoff? What about in-flight writes?

Sasha: Good Q. Plan: keep a short fencing_nonce on the ownership token. Writes include owner nonce; on handoff new owner gets a strictly higher nonce. Residency epoch ensures the new owner only serves once it has data. If a write arrives after owner change we detect nonce mismatch and either forward or reject+retry depending on client mode.

Ajay: What about double-apply if both nodes briefly accept writes? Is forwarding sync or best-effort?

Sasha: We intentionally avoid sync waiting to reduce tail latency. Forwarding is best-effort RPC + retry window. To prevent double-apply we rely on idempotent apply (op_id) at the storage layer + the fencing_nonce check: owner with lower nonce will refuse new applies. If both accept before fence propagation, the idempotency and op dedupe will handle it.

Chen: Eviction semantics — how do we avoid hot-key thrash if residency flips frequently?

Sasha: Add a soft_demote flag + demote grace window. Eviction sets soft_demote=true and starts a grace_ms timer. Read path still serves (with potentially higher cost) during grace; repeated hot reads trigger prefetch to the new owner and accelerate handoff. The goal is reduce oscillation and allow hot keys to stabilize.

Maria: Can you sketch the proto for the token/record?

Sasha: Sure — rough sketch:
```proto
message OwnershipToken {
  string prefix = 1;
  string owner_node = 2;
  uint64 epoch = 3;
  uint64 fencing_nonce = 4;
  repeated string tags = 5;
}
message ResidencyRecord {
  string prefix = 1;
  string node = 2;
  uint64 residency_epoch = 3;
  bool soft_demote = 4;
  uint32 grace_ms = 5;
}
```

Ajay: I like that. Any perf/regression expectations? Rollout plan?

Chen: Proposed rollout: feature flag = "ownership_decouple". Canary 1% -> 10% -> 50% -> 100%. Telemetry to capture: write forward rate, forwarded RPC p99/p95, double-apply rate, evict churn, prefetch rate, tail latency (p99/p999) on read and write, error rates. Also run chaos tests for split/merge.

infra-bot: smoke-tests/ownership_decouple: PASS — unit: 312 tests, integration: 14/14. :white_check_mark:

Sasha: Also need targeted chaos for prefix split/merge and long replay logs. @Ajay @Maria can you pair on integration scenarios next week? :eyes:

Ajay: I can take split/merge + replay determinism tests.

Maria: I'll own handoff/eviction chaos + create a small eval harness for RAWR cases.

Sasha: Thanks — I'll open the rollout PR with the flag, telemetry hooks, and a short deterministic test plan. Will link the PR in the RFC draft.
